   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# ⚗ Honest comparison · same prompt, same seed, same model\n**A** ComfyUI's own KSampler (euler, `simple`, 8 steps) · **B** same Euler solver and 8 steps, but the step spacing measured on YOUR checkpoint · **C** the complete recipe of the starter workflow (two stages, detail, variety, restart, DeGrid).\n\n**How to read it.** All three branches share one Load → LoRA → Prompt chain, one latent size and one fixed seed (424242); NAG is OFF so that only the sampling differs. Open the three saved images at 100 % and compare the same crop. Read each branch's *report*: C makes more model calls than A and B, so it is slower — that is the price of the extra detail, not a free lunch.\n\n**Be fair to yourself.** Run it with 3–4 different seeds and your own prompt before you decide. Without a calibration profile B falls back to an analytic schedule (the report says so): calibrate once with `KREA2_TARATURA` first. Where A already looks right, A is right.\n\n⚗ Idea & direction: AlchemicaMente · code: Claude (Anthropic) · GPL-3.0"
   ]
  }
 ],
